 ],
 "answer_text": "Found 5 pubmed records: On tree longevity. [5], Tree mycorrhizal type and tree diversity shape the forest soil microbiota. [6], Gradient Boosted Tree Approaches for Mapping European Organization for Research and Treatment of Cancer Quality of Life Questionnaire Core 30 Onto 5-Level Version of EQ-5D Index for Patients With Cancer. [7], Tree diversity effects on productivity depend on mycorrhizae and life strategies in a temperate forest experiment. [8] and Seasonal patterns of nonstructural carbohydrate storage and mobilization in two tree species with distinct life-history traits. [9]. \n\nTree Longevity and Senescence\n\nTrees do not appear to die from genetically programmed meristem senescence but rather from extrinsic agents or disturbance events, and their long lifespans depend on life-history trait combinations that resist or avoid external mortality [1]. \n\nMycorrhizal Type and Soil Microbiota\n\nMycorrhizal association type significantly affects fungal but not bacterial alpha diversity in forest soils [2]. Ectomycorrhizal tree species pairs show increased fungal alpha diversity with greater tree diversity, while arbuscular mycorrhizal pairs do not, and the differences between the two types diminish in multi-species mixtures [2]. Higher tree diversity promotes convergence of soil microbial communities [2]. \n\nMycorrhizae and Productivity\n\nEctomycorrhizal communities show low initial productivity with increasing increment over time and strong biodiversity effects, whereas arbuscular mycorrhizal communities display the opposite pattern [3]. No overyielding occurs when the two mycorrhizal types grow together, at least in young stands [3]. \n\nNonstructural Carbohydrate Dynamics\n\nLarger storage pools are not necessarily associated with more pronounced seasonal fluctuations [4]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: On tree longevity [5]. Pubmed title: Tree mycorrhizal type and tree diversity shape the forest soil microbiota [6]. Pubmed title: Gradient Boosted Tree Approaches for Mapping European Organization for Research and Treatment of Cancer Quality of Life Questionnaire Core 30 Onto 5-Level Version of EQ-5D Index for Patients With Cancer [7]. Pubmed title: Tree diversity effects on productivity depend on mycorrhizae and life strategies in a temperate forest experiment [8]. Pubmed title: Seasonal patterns of nonstructural carbohydrate storage and mobilization in two tree species with distinct life-history traits [9]. "
}